I propose testing the 'conformance.kernel.recovered-from-prose' kernel with the 'conformance.transform.prose-after' transform. The catalogue shows that adding prose before the object (conformance.transform.prose-before) causes this kernel to move to true, as the harness must then recover the object from prose rather than reading it as strict JSON. I expect that adding prose after the object will similarly trigger a move to 'true', as the presence of trailing text prevents the reply from being strict JSON, forcing the recovery mechanism to engage.